<title>USA: US West unit may issue $2.0 bln in debt.</title>
<headline>US West unit may issue $2.0 bln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>US West Capital Funding, a unit of U S West Inc, is expected to issue a $2.0 billion four-part debt offering next week via Merrill Lynch &amp; Co, corporate bond syndicate sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;The roadshow (US West Capital) kicks off on Monday, said one high-grade syndicate source. &quot;It looks like the deal will price by the end of next week.&quot;</p>
<p>The offering is expected to consist of five-year, 10-year, 30-year and 40-year maturities, and is rated A2/BBB-plus, sources added.</p>
<p>--Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675</p>
